@startuml SD-01 User Authentication
!theme plain
title SD-01 — User Authentication (UC-01)
actor "School User" as User
boundary "LoginView\n(Desktop UI)" as UI
control "AuthenticationService\n(Business Logic)" as Auth
entity "UserRepository\n(Data Access)" as Repo
database "Central Database" as DB

User -> UI : Enter username and password
User -> UI : Click Login
UI -> UI : Validate required fields
alt Missing required fields
  UI --> User : Display validation message
else Input complete
  UI -> Auth : authenticate(username, password)
  Auth -> Repo : findByUsername(username)
  Repo -> DB : Query account and password hash
  DB --> Repo : Account record or not found
  Repo --> Auth : Account record or not found
  alt Account not found / disabled / invalid password
    Auth --> UI : AuthenticationFailed
    UI --> User : Show generic login error
  else Credentials valid and account active
    Auth -> Repo : loadRolesAndPermissions(userId)
    Repo -> DB : Query active roles and permissions
    DB --> Repo : Authorized roles and permissions
    Repo --> Auth : Authorized roles and permissions
    Auth -> Auth : Establish application session
    Auth --> UI : Authenticated session context
    UI --> User : Open authorized dashboard
  end
end
note over Auth,DB
Password verification occurs in the business logic.
Only password hashes are stored; never return them to the UI.
Authentication failures must not disclose account existence.
end note
@enduml
